@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix foundation: <http://foundation.local/ontology/> .

# =============================================================================
# InformationObject
# =============================================================================
# Data, documents, or encoded knowledge
#
# Version: 0.1.0
# License: GNU GPL
# =============================================================================

foundation:InformationObject a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf foundation:DigitalThing ;
    rdfs:label "Information Object" ;
    rdfs:comment "Digital data, documents, or encoded knowledge" ;
    foundation:icon "description" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso """
Information objects are digital representations of knowledge or data.

Examples:
- A PDF document (this ontology specification)
- A database record (user profile data)
- Source code (FOUNDATION codebase)
- A scientific paper
- A user manual
- An invoice (digital or scanned)
- A contract document

Note: InformationObject is a subclass of DigitalThing, meaning all information
objects inherit the ability to have file attachments via foundation:hasFile.
""" .
